1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:10,677
Custom parts is the CAM side: draw a part, then machine it. Here: a painted sign for the Goldbergs.

2
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:31,113
The dashed rectangle is the panel. First, set its name, size and material in Properties.

3
00:00:31,113 --> 00:00:36,512
Drawing tools are on the left. Rounded rectangle, with a 1" corner radius...

4
00:00:36,512 --> 00:00:42,975
...and type the points: first corner 0,0, then @24,10 means 24" across and 10" up.

5
00:00:42,975 --> 00:00:46,754
Use as part outline makes this the shape the machine cuts out.

6
00:00:46,754 --> 00:00:53,603
The starting rectangle already matched 24" x 10", but it is no longer the outline: click it and press Delete.

7
00:00:53,603 --> 00:01:03,391
A plain rectangle for the recessed panel: corner 3,2, size 18 by 6.

8
00:01:03,391 --> 00:01:13,517
A circle for the hanging hole: centre 1-1/2, 5 and a 5/32" radius (5/16" hole).

9
00:01:13,517 --> 00:01:27,893
Text: type the words, set the height, then give the start of the baseline.

10
00:01:27,893 --> 00:01:38,965
You can also draw with the mouse. Lines: click points, Enter to finish.

11
00:01:38,965 --> 00:01:43,004
Not wanted? Undo takes it back. Redo brings it again.

12
00:01:43,004 --> 00:01:53,065
Wheel to zoom in on a detail; Zoom to fit shows the whole part again.
